@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Creating a Microsoft Azure Account";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">To start using Azure DevOps, you first need to create a Microsoft Azure account. Follow these steps to set up your Azure account and gain access to Azure DevOps services.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Step-by-Step Guide to Creating a Microsoft Azure Account</h2>
        <p>Follow these simple steps to create your Microsoft Azure account:</p>

        <div class="row align-items-center">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Step 1: Go to the Azure Portal</h4>
                <p>Visit the official Microsoft Azure website: <a href="https://azure.microsoft.com/" target="_blank">azure.microsoft.com</a> and click on the "Start free" button.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/media/index/azure-signup.png" alt="Azure Signup Page" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Signup Page</small></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/media/index/azure-signin.png" alt="Sign in with Microsoft Account" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Sign in with Microsoft Account</small></p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Step 2: Sign in with a Microsoft Account</h4>
                <p>If you already have a Microsoft account (Outlook, Hotmail, Xbox, etc.), sign in. If not, create a new account by following the on-screen instructions.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Step 3: Provide Account Details</h4>
                <p>Fill in your personal details, verify your phone number, and enter your payment method (required for verification, but you won’t be charged for free services).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/media/index/azure-account-details.png" alt="Azure Account Details" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Enter your details to set up your Azure account</small></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
            <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
                <img src="https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/media/index/azure-dashboard.png" alt="Azure Portal Dashboard" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
                <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Portal Dashboard</small></p>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <h4>Step 4: Access the Azure Portal</h4>
                <p>Once your account is created, log in to the <a href="https://portal.azure.com/" target="_blank">Azure Portal</a>. This is the central dashboard where you can manage all Azure services.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Creating a Microsoft Azure account is the first step towards using Azure DevOps and other cloud services. Once set up, you can start configuring projects, setting up repositories, and automating deployments using Azure DevOps.
        </p>
        <p>
            Now that your Azure account is ready, the next step is to **set up an Azure DevOps organization** to manage your projects.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-end mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("SettingUpAnAzureDevOpsOrganization", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Setting up an Azure DevOps Organization &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
